---
/**
 * `/privacy` — DRAFT for attorney review.
 *
 * Written from what the site actually does, not from a template: the inquiry
 * form's real field list, the Google Maps embed that loads on /commute, SES and
 * Google Workspace, and the camera system. SEC-008 requires the Maps disclosure
 * before launch, because the map loads without the visitor opting in.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import { isTbd } from '../lib/fact';
import { site, home } from '../data/site.config';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, who it is shared with, and how to reach us about it.">
  <section class="wrap stack measure">
    <h1 class="display-l">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no accounts, no logins and no advertising. It collects what you type into the
      inquiry form and nothing else. Loading the map page shares your IP address with Google.
    </p>

    <h2>What the inquiry form collects</h2>
    <p>
      Your name, email address, and optionally your phone number, role and facility. Your intended
      contract start and length, how many people will stay, whether you are bringing a pet or need
      parking, and anything you write in the message box.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use it to answer your inquiry. It is sent to {site.contact.email} and is not sold, rented or
      shared for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>What it deliberately does not collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site asks your age, date of birth, marital status, household make-up, income,
      employment history, or immigration or citizenship status. There is no rental application on this
      website — the application is handled separately, and screening information belongs there, not here.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else sees data, and when</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google.</strong> The home page loads a Street View image and the commute page embeds
        Google Maps. Loading either sends your IP address and browser details to Google under their own
        privacy policy. This happens without you clicking anything.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Amazon Web Services.</strong> The inquiry form posts to our own endpoint on AWS, which
        emails us the contents. Server logs record the request time, the origin and the requesting IP
        address. They do not record what you typed.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Google Workspace.</strong> Our email runs on it, so inquiries land there.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub.</strong> Hosts these pages and may log requests.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics. The embedded Google map may set its
      own cookies once it loads.
    </p>

    <h2>Cameras at the property</h2>
    <p>
      This concerns residents rather than visitors to this website. A {home.security.system} camera
      system covers the entrances and the outside of the building —
      {' '}{home.security.cameras.map((c) => `${c.count} ${c.type.toLowerCase()}`).join(' and ')}.
      {' '}{home.security.neverCovered} {home.security.residentAccess} Footage is retained for a
      limited period and reviewed only in connection with an incident at the property.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep inquiries</h2>
    <p>{isTbd(site.inquiryRetention) ? "We keep inquiry emails only as long as needed to answer them and keep a record of the conversation. Write to us to have yours deleted." : <Fact value={site.inquiryRetention} />}</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Write to {site.contact.email} to ask what we hold about you, to correct it, or to have it deleted.
      We will respond {site.response.commitment}. You can also simply email or call instead of using the
      form.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>{site.contact.name} · {site.contact.email} · {site.contact.phone}</p>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  section { padding-block: var(--s12) var(--s8); }
  .draft { border-left: 3px solid var(--brick); padding-left: var(--s4); }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--s8); }
  ul { padding-left: var(--s6); }
  li + li { margin-top: var(--s2); }
</style>
